  "note": "Issue #627: the racer, sold only at Skrugs's (his card's sale.models). An open-wheel race car with no wheels. Speeder classes: the light class (the Sand-boxer is the middle one, the box truck the heavy one): the quickest off the line, the sharpest turn and the hardest boost, a little faster than a stock Sand-boxer flat out, and a glass hull (half a Sand-boxer's health: four laser bolts, two seekers or two mines). Same HoverModel, hover, ramps and twin lasers as the Sand-boxer. shop_groups: the bench sells it the shared parts (performance, race gear, the Grav Lifter: speeder_upgrades.json shared_groups) and its own paint jobs (issue #628: look.paints, recolours of its one model from content/look/vehicle_models.json: race white and red, black and gold, desert orange, sold at Dorrin's and Skrugs's bench as paint parts with \"model\": \"racer\"; new ones roll round sold_paints; the Remnant's black and red is ready but not sold). scrap_base: what Dorrin pays for it before paint. Issue #628: look.scene is its Hyper3D body (two booms either side of a bubble-canopy race hull) and the hull collider is the model's shape; look.parts is the glowing arc between the boom tips, bolted on because Rodin draws thin beams badly; look.stand_in (the forked, bubble-canopy primitive the Hyper3D brief was drawn from) is the fallback with a box hull. label is a make and model from the name lists (content/core/names/craft.json). show_driver: its cockpit is open, so you stay visible in the driver's seat while you ride it (in whatever outfit you wear), sat at the bars (BodyAnimator.sit_pose), hands on look.yoke, the ship cockpit's yoke (CockpitView.build_yoke) scaled and placed in the speeder's frame, fixed; the other speeders hide you.",
